.TP
.B completion bash|zsh|fish
Print the completion script of that shell on stdout. The script asks
.B "tacctl __complete"
for the words. Live names
(users, groups, scopes, backends, listeners, backups) come from
.BR "sudo -n tacctl" ,
which needs root or the NOPASSWD rule of
.BR "config sudoers install" ;
without it only fixed words are completed. Install and upgrade write the
bash script to
.IR /etc/bash_completion.d/tacctl ;
the zsh and fish scripts are only printed: redirect them to
.I ~/.zfunc/_tacctl
(with that directory on
.B fpath
before
.BR compinit )
or to
.IR ~/.config/fish/completions/tacctl.fish .
