Requires: \fBsuperuser\fR.
.RE
.\" END GENERATED: command scope auth-method
.SS Per-scope AAA method-list order \fB(tacctl scope aaa-order)\fR
.TP
.BI "scope aaa-order " scope " [" tacacs-first | local-first ]
Show or set the order of methods in the Cisco
.B aaa authentication login
/
.B aaa authorization
lines and Junos
.B system authentication-order
emitted by
.B "config cisco --scope " \fIscope\fR
and
.B "config juniper --scope " \fIscope\fR .
Default (unset)
.B tacacs-first
keeps TACACS+ authoritative (local only kicks in on server outage).
.B local-first
lets a local break-glass account authenticate even
while TACACS+ is reachable: any local username that collides with a
TACACS+ user wins locally on devices in this scope, so scope
local accounts to emergency / break-glass credentials only.
The change takes effect for the next
.B "config cisco"
/
.B "config juniper"
render of the named scope; existing device configs are unchanged
until the new method-list stanzas are pushed.
