when the plan has no back\-out to write (each says so on standard error).
.B "\-\-plain \-\-converge"
says on standard error why a device has no cleanup file (deferred to after the
first region, refused, nothing to remove). Several devices print the cover
page first, one line per device
.RB ( consistent ,
.BR "needs change" ,
.BR "NOT consistent, nothing to paste" ,
.BR "cannot be planned" ),
then the outputs separated by a rule;
.B \-\-plain
of several devices needs
.BR \-\-out\-dir .
.PP
A device cannot be planned, with the reason on standard error and exit 1, when
it was never pulled, was pulled more than
.B stale\-days
ago, whose last pull failed, a Cisco device whose syntax is unknown, or one
whose plan has nothing to paste because a section was refused (a WTI unit
whose IP tables list is refused and that has no step is one of these).
Exit status 0 when the outputs were made, 1 when a device cannot be planned, 2
for wrong arguments (and, with
.BR \-\-exit\-code ,
when a device needs a change and none could not be planned), 130 when
interrupted. An engineer plans the devices of their own scopes, and a section
their login's class cannot commit
.RB ( EN\-CLASS :
the server, accounting,
.BR login ,
.BR snmp )
is not in the region, with one report line saying so. Every device is logged
.RB ( "auth.info device config plan user= device= status= sections= converge= secrets= out=" ,
never a value). The Cisco report states which output has been tested on a
device.
