(pull, diff, plan, forget) Every device of yours that a scope covers.
.TP
\fB\-\-scope\fR \fI<scope>\fR
(pull, diff, plan, list) Only the devices of that scope.
.TP
\fB\-\-vendor\fR \fIcisco|juniper|wti\fR
(pull, diff, plan, list) Only that vendor's devices.
.TP
\fB\-\-stale\fR
(pull, diff, plan, list) Only the devices never read, last read in failure, or differing.
.TP
\fB\-\-transport\fR \fIauto|netconf|ssh\fR
(pull, diff, plan) NETCONF where the device answers (auto, default), NETCONF only, or the ssh command line only; (list) netconf, ssh or none: only the devices last read over that transport (none: never read).
.TP
\fB\-\-concurrency\fR \fI<n>\fR
Read at most n devices at once (never above device.config.max_concurrency).
.TP
\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fI<seconds>\fR
Per device, connect included (10\-600; default device.config.timeout).
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-failures\fR \fI<n>\fR
Stop starting devices after n failures.
.TP
\fB\-\-server\fR \fI<address|name>\fR
The address the devices are told to authenticate against, for devices behind a translating firewall (not stored).
.TP
\fB\-\-source\fR \fI<address>\fR
The address this server reaches the devices from (not stored).
.TP
\fB\-\-login\fR \fI<local\-user>\fR
(pull, diff \-\-pull, plan \-\-pull) Superusers, one registered Junos device with a pinned key: log in as that local account of the device instead of you (any local account, a break\-glass one included; only root is handled apart: a device never read as you, through its csh wrapper); its password is asked once on the terminal and never kept or cached.
.TP
\fB\-\-pull\fR
Read the devices first (takes the pull options); the plan is made from that pull.
.TP
\fB\-\-section\fR \fI<list>\fR
Only these sections: aaa, roles, mgmt\-acl, snmp, system (the report still names the others).
.TP
\fB\-\-converge\fR
Add the cleanup of a device with nothing else to paste: the region that removes the old servers and the like (a device with a first region gets that and a line to plan again after the paste; a WTI unit: the read/write community and the other protocol's switch).
.TP
\fB\-\-secrets\fR
Type every secret of the planned sections, also the ones the device has (a WTI step names the command that shows the value unless given).
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-secrets\fR
Leave each secret as a marked line to fill in (no plain form; a WTI step already does).
.TP
\fB\-\-plain\fR
The statements of one device alone, for 'load set' (\-\-converge: two files, with \-\-out or \-\-out\-dir); a WTI unit has none.
.TP
\fB\-\-backout\fR
Only the back\-out region (what puts the pulled lines back; the one kept from the plan once a later pull replaced them; not with \-\-pull).
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
One object per device: the findings, the region, the cleanup and the back\-out; values elided.
.TP
\fB\-\-out\fR \fI<file>\fR
Write one device's output to a file (0600).
.TP
\fB\-\-out\-dir\fR \fI<dir>\fR
One file per device (<name>.txt, .set with \-\-plain, .json with \-\-json; each plan's .backout.txt) and COVER.txt, 0600 in a 0700 directory.
