.SS Login console \fB(tacctl console)\fR
The login console
.RB ( tacctl\-console )
is the login shell of tacctl users on the tacctl server: tacctl commands and
ssh to registered devices, nothing else. It is on for every tier by default
(the defaults apply while
.I /etc/tacctl/console.yaml
is absent); local accounts that are not tacctl users are never touched. These
commands change
.I console.yaml
only, after a snapshot (mode 0600; backup diff and restore include it), and
never an account or sshd: the accounts' login shells and sshd's drop-in follow
it when the provisioning of this server applies it
.RB ( "host sync" " of the host enrolled with " \-\-local ).
Every change to the tier switches, a user override, agent forwarding or the
forwarding tiers prints
.BI "Apply to the accounts: tacctl host sync " name\fR.
The idle timeout, the ssh escape, the space completion, the system shell and
the password cache are read by each console session when it starts; open
sessions keep their settings.
.TP
.B console
With no subcommand (or with
.BR help ),
prints a usage summary and exits 0.
.TP
.B console show
The tiers' switches, the settings, and for each user of the scope of the host
enrolled with
.B \-\-local
the tier, the effective shell
.RB ( console
or
.BR bash )
and why
.RI ( "user override" ", " "tier readonly" ", " "tier readonly disabled" ).
Then the state of the server's pieces: the
.I /usr/local/bin/tacctl\-console
symlink, the
.I /etc/shells
line, sshd's drop-in, the engineer tier's own drop-in (its absence or a
difference from this release's is a red warning too), and what
.B "sshd \-T \-C user="\fIuser\fR
reports for a console user
.RB ( allowtcpforwarding ,
.BR allowagentforwarding ,
.BR forcecommand ,
.BR pubkeyauthentication ).
A red warning appears when the drop-in is missing, sshd does not force the
console, still allows forwarding, or allows key logins. A server not enrolled
with
.B \-\-local
says so and lists no users.
